      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:3:184:8",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ يَعْقُوبُ لِابْنِهِ يَا بُنَيَّ لَا تَزْنِ فَإِنَّ الطَّائِرَ لَوْ زَنَى لَتَنَاثَرَ رِيشُهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Fazzal, from Abdullah Bin Maymoun Al Qaddah, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Yaqoub<sup>as</sup> said to his<sup>as</sup> son<sup>as</sup>: ‘Do not commit adultery, for the bird, if it commits adultery, its feathers fall off’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "8. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn Faddal from ‘Abd Allah ibn Maymun al-Qaddah who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that Ya’qub said to his son, ‘O son, do not commit fornication; even if a bird commits fornication it loses its feathers.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
